  speakerName: Klara
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Let''s begin counting in Ilokano.

    The word ''maysa'' means
    ''one.''

    You use it when counting a single person or object.

    For example,
    if you see one chest, you can say ''maysa.''

    Listen carefully: maysa.

    Now,
    try saying ''maysa'' yourself.'
